msgid "Connect the console to this router"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wired or Wi-Fi. The console must get its address from this router (DHCP). PS5 has different MAC addresses for LAN cable and Wi-Fi; both are detected automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set DNS to \"Automatic\""
msgstr ""

msgid "PS5: Settings → Network → Settings → Set Up Internet Connection → your network → Advanced Settings → DNS Settings: Automatic. Manual DNS is also redirected, but \"Automatic\" is the most reliable, especially with podkop."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn off automatic updates"
msgstr ""

msgid "PS5: Settings → System → System Software → System Software Update and Settings → turn off \"Download Update Files Automatically\" and \"Install Update Files Automatically\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "Delete an update that was already downloaded"
msgstr ""

msgid "The router cannot remove files that are already on the console. If a \"system update downloaded\" notice is shown, delete that download on the console before it is installed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable blocking here and check the console list"
msgstr ""

msgid "The console appears in the list above with status \"Blocked\". If you have several consoles, all are blocked; use \"Exclude\" for the ones that may update."
msgstr ""

msgid "Restart the console"
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn it off completely (not rest mode) and on again so it forgets cached DNS answers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check"
msgstr ""

msgid "PS5: Settings → System → System Software → System Software Update and Settings → Update System Software → Update Using Internet. The console must report an error instead of finding a new version. Games, patches and PSN keep working."
msgstr ""

msgid "How to set up the console"
msgstr ""

msgid "Limits: a console connected to another network (phone hotspot, another router) or updated from a USB drive is not covered by the router."
msgstr ""

msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

msgid "General"
msgstr ""

msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgid "Blocking mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "<b>Consoles only</b>: rules apply only to PlayStation consoles (by MAC), all other devices are untouched. <b>Whole network</b>: rules apply to every client of the selected networks; use it if the console MAC changes or you want no exceptions. podkop and zapret keep working in both modes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Consoles only (by MAC address)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Whole network"
msgstr ""

msgid "Detect consoles automatically"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finds consoles by the Sony Interactive Entertainment MAC prefix and by device name (DHCP leases and ARP). New consoles are added as soon as they get an address."
msgstr ""

msgid "Networks"
msgstr ""

msgid "Networks where consoles (or, in \"Whole network\" mode, all clients) are connected. Usually \"lan\"; add a guest network if the console uses it."
msgstr ""

msgid "DNS block"
msgstr ""

msgid "dnsmasq answers NXDOMAIN for the update domains. Always network-wide; no other device uses these domains."
msgstr ""

msgid "DNS redirect"
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer every DNS request of the console from the router, even with manual DNS on the console."
msgstr ""

msgid "Strict DNS"
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop console DNS requests to external servers instead of redirecting them. \"Auto\" enables it only for consoles that podkop routes completely, because podkop would otherwise intercept their DNS first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Auto (only when podkop routes the console)"
msgstr ""

msgid "On"
msgstr ""

msgid "Block DoT / DoQ"
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop encrypted DNS on port 853."
msgstr ""

msgid "Block DoH resolvers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop connections to well-known public DNS-over-HTTPS resolvers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Block update servers by IP (L3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop update server addresses directly. The list is refreshed by the router in the background."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer every DNS request in the network from the router. Compatible with podkop (it needs clients to use the router DNS anyway)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop DNS requests to external servers for every client. Devices with manual DNS lose name resolution; enable only if needed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop port 853 for every client. Browsers and phones with \"Private DNS\" fall back to normal DNS."
msgstr ""

msgid "Drop connections to public DoH resolvers for every client. Some apps may show DNS errors before falling back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Update servers share CDN addresses with other sites; for the whole network this can block unrelated content. Off by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "Refresh interval (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "How often the update server address list and the console list are refreshed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Blocked domains"
msgstr ""

msgid "Blocked together with all subdomains. Default: ps5.update.playstation.net (system software only; games and patches use other domains)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Resolvers for the address list"
msgstr ""

msgid "Public DNS servers the router asks for update server addresses."
msgstr ""

msgid "Consoles added by hand"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add a console that is not detected automatically, or keep a detected console unblocked by adding it with \"Block\" turned off. The buttons in the status list above do the same."
msgstr ""

msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

msgid "PS5 Update Block"
msgstr ""

msgid "Blocks PlayStation 5 system software updates on the router. Games, patches, PSN and all other devices keep working."
msgstr ""


msgid "Payload sent to %s (%d bytes) and deleted from the router."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sending the payload failed: %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Payload upload failed: %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Upload a homebrew payload (ELF/bin) and send it to this console on port %d. The console must already run a payload loader. The file is deleted from the router right after sending."
msgstr ""

msgid "Send payload"
msgstr ""

msgid "Payload port"
msgstr ""

msgid "TCP port the console's homebrew payload loader listens on. Default 9021. Used by the \"Send payload\" button in the console list."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check port"
msgstr ""

msgid "Check whether the console is listening for payloads on port %d (one-shot loaders may treat the check as a connection)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Port %d on %s is open: the payload loader is ready."
msgstr ""

msgid "Port %d on %s is closed. Start the payload loader on the console first."
msgstr ""

msgid "No IP address for this console; turn it on and connect it to this router."
msgstr ""

msgid "Port check failed."
msgstr ""

msgid "The payload loader is not listening on port %d of %s; nothing was sent. Start the loader on the console and try again."
msgstr ""

msgid "What to block (DNS)"
msgstr ""

msgid "<b>Updates only</b>: system software update servers; games, the store and PSN keep working. <b>All PSN servers</b>: also blocks downloads (incl. games), store, sign-in and social — the console is cut off from Sony. <b>Custom</b>: only the list below."
msgstr ""

msgid "Updates only (recommended)"
msgstr ""

msgid "All PSN servers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom list only"
msgstr ""

msgid "Extra blocked domains"
msgstr ""

msgid "Blocked together with all subdomains, on top of the preset above (for \"Custom\", this is the whole list)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Forced to %s. "
msgstr ""

msgid "Forced to the router. "
msgstr ""

msgid "Force DNS to this server"
msgstr ""

msgid "Send the console's DNS to this server instead of the router (overrides podkop/AdGuard). Leave empty to use the router's dnsmasq. With a non-router server the built-in DNS block does not apply to the console — blocking then relies on the IP/DoT/DoH layers or that server's own filtering."
msgstr ""

